error BYN2201: a `string` cannot be indexed

  2 │ let first = name[0]
    │                 ^^^ strings have no indexer
    │
  help: read a byte, slice, or take characters; `string` is UTF-8, so position 0 is not a character:
          `name.bytes[0]`       the byte at offset 0 (applied below)
          `name[a..b]`          the text between byte offsets a and b
          `name.runes.take(n)`  the first n runes
          `name.graphemes`      user-perceived characters
    │ 2 │ let first = name.bytes[0]
    │   │                 ++++++
